hostname r4
!
ip routing
!
! -------------------------------------------------------
! Node: r4  (Stub Area 2 router)
!
! This router lives entirely in OSPF Area 2, which is a stub area.
! In a stub area, external LSAs (Type-5) are not flooded; instead
! r3 (the ABR) injects a default route into the area.
! Both r3 and r4 must agree on the stub configuration.
!
! What you need to configure here:
!   - OSPF process "CORE" with router-id 10.0.0.4
!   - ip ospf area 2 on Ethernet1 (link to r3)
!   - ip ospf area 2 on Loopback0, marked passive
!   - Declare Area 2 as a stub area in the OSPF process:
!       area 2 stub
!     (must match r3's configuration)
! Hint:
!   interface Loopback0
!    ip ospf area 2
!   !
!   interface Ethernet1
!    ip ospf area 2
!   !
!   router ospf 1
!    ospf router-id 10.0.0.4
!    passive-interface Loopback0
!    area 2 stub
! -------------------------------------------------------
!
interface Loopback0
 ip address 10.0.0.4/32
!
interface Ethernet1
 no switchport
 description to r3
 ip address 10.1.34.2/30
!
